---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

/* External links for the hero buttons (leave empty to disable a button) */
const projectUrl = 'https://amaesc.github.io/Space-Apps-Project/';
const demoUrl = 'https://youtu.be/9GTanSEWZUc';
const repoUrl = 'https://github.com/amaesc/Space-Apps-Project';
---

<Layout>
	<header>
		<div class="header-tools">
			<div class="language-switch" role="group" aria-label="Language selector">
				<button type="button" data-language="en" aria-pressed="true">EN</button>
				<button type="button" data-language="es" aria-pressed="false">ES</button>
			</div>
			<img
				class="header-logo"
				src="/images/flamin-mascot.png"
				alt="FireData logo"
				data-en="FireData logo"
				data-es="Logotipo de FireData"
			/>
		</div>

		<p
			class="header-kicker"
			data-en="FireData · NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026"
			data-es="FireData · NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026"
		>
			FireData · NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026
		</p>
		<h1
			data-en="FireData: Harmonization of MODIS and VIIRS Hot Spots"
			data-es="FireData: Armonización de puntos calientes MODIS y VIIRS"
		>
			FireData: Harmonization of MODIS and VIIRS Hot Spots
		</h1>
		<p
			class="header-description"
			data-en="We harmonize two decades of MODIS and VIIRS satellite detections into a consistent burn calendar, forecast where fire is most likely in the coming weeks, and fill satellite gaps with low-cost IoT field stations."
			data-es="Armonizamos dos décadas de detecciones satelitales de MODIS y VIIRS en un calendario de quemas consistente, pronosticamos dónde es más probable que haya fuego en las próximas semanas y cubrimos los huecos de los satélites con estaciones IoT de bajo costo en campo."
		>
			We harmonize two decades of MODIS and VIIRS satellite detections into a
			consistent burn calendar, forecast where fire is most likely in the coming
			weeks, and fill satellite gaps with low-cost IoT field stations.
		</p>
		<div class="hero-actions">
			{projectUrl ? (
				<a
					class="button-web"
					href={projectUrl}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					data-en="Web project"
					data-es="Proyecto web"
				>
					Web project
				</a>
			) : (
				<button
					class="button-web"
					type="button"
					disabled
					data-en="Web project"
					data-es="Proyecto web"
				>
					Web project
				</button>
			)}
			{demoUrl ? (
				<a
					class="button-demo"
					href={demoUrl}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					data-en="View demo"
					data-es="Ver demo"
				>
					View demo
				</a>
			) : (
				<button
					class="button-demo"
					type="button"
					disabled
					data-en="View demo"
					data-es="Ver demo"
				>
					View demo
				</button>
			)}
			{repoUrl ? (
				<a
					class="button-repo"
					href={repoUrl}
					target="_blank"
					rel="noopener noreferrer"
					data-en="GitHub repository"
					data-es="Repositorio en GitHub"
				>
					GitHub repository
				</a>
			) : (
				<button
					class="button-repo"
					type="button"
					disabled
					data-en="GitHub repository"
					data-es="Repositorio en GitHub"
				>
					GitHub repository
				</button>
			)}
		</div>
	</header>

	<main>
		<section>
			<h2 data-en="The challenge" data-es="La problemática">The challenge</h2>
			<div class="content-with-image">
				<div>
					<p
						data-en="For more than 20 years, MODIS and VIIRS satellite sensors have recorded hotspots around the world. However, their data cannot be directly compared because of differences in spatial resolution, sensitivity, and observation times. As MODIS approaches the end of its service life and is replaced by VIIRS, the lack of a method to unify both time series threatens to fragment nearly a decade of history and leave emergency teams without a continuous climate record."
						data-es="Durante más de 20 años, los sensores satelitales MODIS y VIIRS han registrado puntos calientes en todo el planeta. Sin embargo, sus datos no son directamente comparables debido a diferencias en resolución espacial, sensibilidad y horarios de observación. Con MODIS llegando al final de su vida útil para ser reemplazado por VIIRS, la falta de un método que unifique ambas series amenaza con fragmentar casi una década de historial y dejar a los equipos de emergencia sin un registro climático continuo."
					>
						For more than 20 years, MODIS and VIIRS satellite sensors have
						recorded hotspots around the world. However, their data cannot be
						directly compared because of differences in spatial resolution,
						sensitivity, and observation times. As MODIS approaches the end of
						its service life and is replaced by VIIRS, the lack of a method to
						unify both time series threatens to fragment nearly a decade of
						history and leave emergency teams without a continuous climate
						record.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="Three critical operational challenges add to this historical gap:"
						data-es="A esta brecha histórica se suman tres obstáculos operativos críticos:"
					>
						Three critical operational challenges add to this historical gap:
					</p>
					<ul>
						<li>
							<strong
								data-en="Data latency and blind spots:"
								data-es="Latencia y ceguera de datos:"
								>Data latency and blind spots:</strong
							>
							<span
								data-en="Near-real-time detection is only available for the United States and Canada. Elsewhere, global reports take 1 to 3 hours to arrive, with delays worsened by areas without continuous satellite coverage or connectivity loss at remote stations."
								data-es="Mientras que la detección en minutos solo está disponible para Estados Unidos y Canadá, en el resto del mundo los reportes globales tardan entre 1 y 3 horas en llegar, agravado por zonas sin cobertura satelital continua o pérdida de conectividad en estaciones remotas."
							>
								Near-real-time detection is only available for the United States
								and Canada. Elsewhere, global reports take 1 to 3 hours to
								arrive, with delays worsened by areas without continuous
								satellite coverage or connectivity loss at remote stations.
							</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong
								data-en="Uncertainty about fire origin:"
								data-es="Incertidumbre sobre el origen:"
								>Uncertainty about fire origin:</strong
							>
							<span
								data-en="Satellite records detect heat, but cannot determine on their own whether a fire was caused by a natural phenomenon or human activity."
								data-es="Los registros satelitales detectan el calor, pero no distinguen por sí solos si el fuego fue causado por un fenómeno natural o por actividad humana."
							>
								Satellite records detect heat, but cannot determine on their own
								whether a fire was caused by a natural phenomenon or human
								activity.
							</span>
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong
								data-en="Critical impact in northern Mexico:"
								data-es="Impacto crítico en el norte de México:"
								>Critical impact in northern Mexico:</strong
							>
							<span
								data-en="In regions such as Chihuahua, where the State Department of Rural Development (SDR) reports 289 forest fires and 43,206.76 hectares affected so far this year, most incidents are human-caused. Identifying likely causes is essential for prevention and monitoring."
								data-es="En regiones como Chihuahua, donde la Secretaría de Desarrollo Rural (SDR) reporta 289 incendios forestales y 43,206.76 hectáreas afectadas en lo que va del año, la mayoría de los siniestros tienen origen humano, por lo que identificar causas probables es vital para la prevención y la vigilancia."
							>
								In regions such as Chihuahua, where the State Department of Rural
								Development (SDR) reports 289 forest fires and 43,206.76
								hectares affected so far this year, most incidents are
								human-caused. Identifying likely causes is essential for
								prevention and monitoring.
							</span>
						</li>
					</ul>
				</div>
				<figure class="challenge-image project-image">
					<img
						src="/images/modis-viirs-chihuahua.png"
						alt="Comparison of hotspots detected by MODIS and VIIRS in Chihuahua"
						data-en="Comparison of hotspots detected by MODIS and VIIRS in Chihuahua"
						data-es="Comparación de puntos calientes detectados por MODIS y VIIRS en Chihuahua"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption
						data-en="2026 NASA Space Apps Challenge"
						data-es="2026 NASA Space Apps Challenge"
					>
						2026 NASA Space Apps Challenge
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2
				data-en="Harmonized satellite observations"
				data-es="Observaciones satelitales armonizadas"
			>
				Harmonized satellite observations
			</h2>
			<div class="content-with-image">
				<div>
					<p
						data-en="FireData unifies MODIS and VIIRS records to eliminate sensor discrepancies and prevent gaps in historical continuity."
						data-es="FireData unifica los registros de MODIS y VIIRS para eliminar las discrepancias entre sensores y evitar la pérdida de continuidad histórica."
					>
						FireData unifies MODIS and VIIRS records to eliminate sensor
						discrepancies and prevent gaps in historical continuity.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="Through monthly calibration, uncertainty estimates, and cross-validation, the platform enables consistent comparisons across time periods and builds a reliable calendar of thermal activity."
						data-es="Mediante calibración mensual, estimaciones de incertidumbre y validación cruzada, la plataforma permite comparar periodos de forma consistente y construir un calendario confiable de actividad térmica a lo largo del tiempo."
					>
						Through monthly calibration, uncertainty estimates, and
						cross-validation, the platform enables consistent comparisons
						across time periods and builds a reliable calendar of thermal
						activity.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="project-image">
					<img
						src="/images/demo-stand.jpeg"
						alt="FireData stand showing the fire map platform and the IoT weather station"
						data-en="FireData stand showing the fire map platform and the IoT weather station"
						data-es="Stand de FireData con la plataforma del mapa de incendios y la estación meteorológica IoT"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption
						data-en="Demo stand at the Open House with the web app and IoT device"
						data-es="Stand demostrativo en Open House con App Web y dispositivo IoT"
					>
						Demo stand at the Open House with the web app and IoT device
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2
				data-en="Statistical prediction model"
				data-es="Modelo estadístico de predicción"
			>
				Statistical prediction model
			</h2>
			<div class="content-with-image">
				<div>
					<p
						data-en="For each 10 km grid cell, our model estimates the probability of a fire occurring in the next 7 to 14 days. It learns from two decades of harmonized MODIS and VIIRS history and considers recent fires, time since the last fire, nearby activity, and the time of year. It uses only past information and outperforms seasonal baselines in years it has never seen."
						data-es="Nuestro modelo estima, para cada cuadro de 10 km, la probabilidad de que haya un incendio en los próximos 7 a 14 días. Aprende de dos décadas de historia armonizada de MODIS y VIIRS, y considera los incendios recientes, el tiempo desde el último, la actividad cercana y la época del año. Usa solo información pasada y supera a las referencias estacionales en años que nunca vio."
					>
						For each 10 km grid cell, our model estimates the probability of a
						fire occurring in the next 7 to 14 days. It learns from two decades
						of harmonized MODIS and VIIRS history and considers recent fires,
						time since the last fire, nearby activity, and the time of year. It
						uses only past information and outperforms seasonal baselines in
						years it has never seen.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="Its probabilities are calibrated, so a 10% risk means that, in similar cases, a fire occurred roughly 1 out of every 10 times. The result is a risk map that helps fire crews and communities decide where to look first."
						data-es="Sus probabilidades están calibradas, así que un riesgo de 10% significa que, en casos parecidos, hubo fuego más o menos 1 de cada 10 veces. El resultado es un mapa de riesgo que ayuda a brigadas y comunidades a decidir dónde mirar primero."
					>
						Its probabilities are calibrated, so a 10% risk means that, in
						similar cases, a fire occurred roughly 1 out of every 10 times. The
						result is a risk map that helps fire crews and communities decide
						where to look first.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="project-image">
					<img
						src="/images/prediction-model.jpeg"
						alt="Fire risk prediction map for Chihuahua and surrounding regions"
						data-en="Fire risk prediction map for Chihuahua and surrounding regions"
						data-es="Mapa de predicción de riesgo de incendios en Chihuahua y regiones cercanas"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption
						data-en="Predictive model for the next 7 days"
						data-es="Modelo predictivo de los siguientes 7 días"
					>
						Predictive model for the next 7 days
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2
				data-en="Field measurements and continuous backup"
				data-es="Mediciones en campo y respaldo continuo"
			>
				Field measurements and continuous backup
			</h2>
			<div class="content-with-image">
				<div>
					<p
						data-en="To mitigate satellite latency in critical areas, our IoT station collects temperature, humidity, wind, precipitation, and electrical activity directly in the field, calculating local ignition-risk indicators."
						data-es="Para mitigar la latencia satelital en zonas críticas, nuestra estación IoT recopila temperatura, humedad, viento, precipitación y actividad eléctrica directamente en el terreno, calculando indicadores locales de riesgo de ignición."
					>
						To mitigate satellite latency in critical areas, our IoT station
						collects temperature, humidity, wind, precipitation, and electrical
						activity directly in the field, calculating local ignition-risk
						indicators.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="Station data provides continuous backup to detect anomalies and issue early warnings, even without direct satellite coverage."
						data-es="La información de la estación genera un respaldo continuo que permite detectar anomalías y alertas tempranas, incluso en ausencia de cobertura satelital directa."
					>
						Station data provides continuous backup to detect anomalies and
						issue early warnings, even without direct satellite coverage.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="project-image">
					<img
						src="/images/iot-station.jpeg"
						alt="IoT station with environmental sensors for fire-risk monitoring"
						data-en="IoT station with environmental sensors for fire-risk monitoring"
						data-es="Estación IoT con sensores ambientales para monitorear el riesgo de incendios"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption
						data-en="Field monitoring station"
						data-es="Estación de monitoreo en campo"
					>
						Field monitoring station
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="tools">
			<h2
				data-en="Platform tools"
				data-es="Herramientas de la plataforma"
			>
				Platform tools
			</h2>

			<article>
				<h3 data-en="Interactive map" data-es="Mapa interactivo">Interactive map</h3>
				<p
					data-en="Explore areas of interest and filter hotspots by risk level and likely origin."
					data-es="Permite explorar la zona de interés y filtrar puntos calientes según su nivel de riesgo y origen probable."
				>
					Explore areas of interest and filter hotspots by risk level and likely
					origin.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article>
				<h3
					data-en="Activity calendar"
					data-es="Calendario de actividad"
				>
					Activity calendar
				</h3>
				<p
					data-en="Organize the unified history by year and month, view total records, or filter by natural or human origin."
					data-es="Organiza el historial unificado por año y mes, permitiendo visualizar el total de registros o segmentarlos por origen natural o humano."
				>
					Organize the unified history by year and month, view total records, or
					filter by natural or human origin.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article>
				<h3
					data-en="Area monitoring dashboard"
					data-es="Panel de monitoreo por área"
				>
					Area monitoring dashboard
				</h3>
				<p
					data-en="Compare current conditions with historical reference values, highlighting anomalies and early warnings."
					data-es="Compara las condiciones actuales frente a valores históricos de referencia, destacando anomalías y alertas tempranas."
				>
					Compare current conditions with historical reference values,
					highlighting anomalies and early warnings.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article>
				<h3
					data-en="Time-series downloads"
					data-es="Descarga de series de datos"
				>
					Time-series downloads
				</h3>
				<p
					data-en="Export harmonized time series with uncertainty metrics and source-sensor metadata."
					data-es="Facilita la exportación de las series armonizadas junto con sus métricas de incertidumbre y metadatos del sensor de origen."
				>
					Export harmonized time series with uncertainty metrics and
					source-sensor metadata.
				</p>
			</article>

			<article>
				<h3
					data-en="Event technical report (future development)"
					data-es="Ficha técnica por evento (implementaciones futuras)"
				>
					Event technical report (future development)
				</h3>
				<p
					data-en="Will break down the likely origin of each hotspot and the environmental variables supporting the estimate."
					data-es="Desglosará la probabilidad de origen de cada punto caliente junto con las variables ambientales que sustentan el cálculo."
				>
					Will break down the likely origin of each hotspot and the
					environmental variables supporting the estimate.
				</p>
			</article>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2
				data-en="Harmonization pilot project: Mexico"
				data-es="Proyecto piloto de armonización: México"
			>
				Harmonization pilot project: Mexico
			</h2>
			<div class="content-with-image">
				<div>
					<p
						data-en="FireData is a web app that uses NASA FIRMS satellite fire data to build a consistent burning calendar for any region, from 2002 to today. Our goal is to help fire managers, brigades and researchers in underserved regions see when and where fires really happen."
						data-es="FireData es una aplicación web que usa los datos satelitales de incendios de NASA FIRMS para construir un calendario de quemas consistente para cualquier región, desde 2002 hasta hoy. Nuestro objetivo es ayudar a gestores del fuego, brigadas e investigadores en regiones desatendidas a ver cuándo y dónde ocurren realmente los incendios."
					>
						FireData is a web app that uses NASA FIRMS satellite fire data to
						build a consistent burning calendar for any region, from 2002 to
						today. Our goal is to help fire managers, brigades and researchers in
						underserved regions see when and where fires really happen.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="By calibrating NASA's newer VIIRS sensor to match the older MODIS record, region by region, FireData lets users pick an area, see which months and years burned the most, compare this month with the historical average, and download the data. The platform also connects our “estaca”, a low-cost ESP32 field station that reports temperature, humidity, pressure, flame and sound from the ground, between satellite passes."
						data-es="Al calibrar el sensor VIIRS, más reciente, para que coincida con el registro histórico de MODIS, región por región, FireData permite elegir un área, ver qué meses y años tuvieron más incendios, comparar el mes actual con el promedio histórico y descargar los datos. La plataforma también conecta nuestra “estaca”, una estación de campo de bajo costo con ESP32 que reporta temperatura, humedad, presión, flama y sonido desde el terreno, entre pasos de los satélites."
					>
						By calibrating NASA's newer VIIRS sensor to match the older MODIS
						record, region by region, FireData lets users pick an area, see which
						months and years burned the most, compare this month with the
						historical average, and download the data. The platform also connects
						our “estaca”, a low-cost ESP32 field station that reports temperature,
						humidity, pressure, flame and sound from the ground, between satellite
						passes.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="FireData addresses the false jump in fire counts that appears when the two sensors are mixed, and we demonstrate it across all 32 states of Mexico. It would help communities worldwide tell a real fire anomaly from a sensor change, and act earlier."
						data-es="FireData corrige el falso salto en el número de incendios que aparece cuando se mezclan ambos sensores, y lo demostramos en los 32 estados de México. Esto ayudaría a comunidades de todo el mundo a distinguir una anomalía real de incendios de un cambio de sensor, y a actuar antes."
					>
						FireData addresses the false jump in fire counts that appears when the
						two sensors are mixed, and we demonstrate it across all 32 states of
						Mexico. It would help communities worldwide tell a real fire anomaly
						from a sensor change, and act earlier.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="project-image">
					<img
						src="/images/harmonization-pilot.jpeg"
						alt="FireData web app showing NASA active fires across Mexico"
						data-en="FireData web app showing NASA active fires across Mexico"
						data-es="Aplicación web de FireData mostrando los incendios activos de la NASA en todo México"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption
						data-en="FireData web app: harmonized fire data across Mexico"
						data-es="App web de FireData: datos de incendios armonizados en todo México"
					>
						FireData web app: harmonized fire data across Mexico
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2
				data-en="Prediction pilot project: Sierra de Chihuahua"
				data-es="Proyecto piloto de predicción: Sierra de Chihuahua"
			>
				Prediction pilot project: Sierra de Chihuahua
			</h2>
			<div class="content-with-image">
				<div>
					<p
						data-en="We focused the prediction pilot on our own region: the Sierra de Chihuahua, where our team lives and where forest fires have the greatest impact on our communities."
						data-es="Enfocamos el piloto de predicción en nuestra propia región: la Sierra de Chihuahua, donde vive nuestro equipo y donde los incendios forestales tienen mayor impacto en nuestras comunidades."
					>
						We focused the prediction pilot on our own region: the Sierra de
						Chihuahua, where our team lives and where forest fires have the
						greatest impact on our communities.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="Taking Chihuahua's forest-fire situation as a reference, the State Department of Rural Development (SDR) reported 289 forest fires so far this year, preliminarily affecting 43,206.76 hectares. The project proposes a pilot deployment in the Sierra de Chihuahua, combining an IoT station with satellite and meteorological backup."
						data-es="Tomando como referencia la problemática forestal de Chihuahua, la Secretaría de Desarrollo Rural (SDR) informó que en lo que va del presente año se han registrado 289 incendios forestales en la entidad, los cuales han afectado preliminarmente una superficie de 43 mil 206.76 hectáreas. El proyecto plantea un despliegue piloto en la Sierra de Chihuahua con monitoreo híbrido (estación IoT más respaldo satelital y meteorológico)."
					>
						Taking Chihuahua's forest-fire situation as a reference, the State
						Department of Rural Development (SDR) reported 289 forest fires so
						far this year, preliminarily affecting 43,206.76 hectares. The
						project proposes a pilot deployment in the Sierra de Chihuahua,
						combining an IoT station with satellite and meteorological backup.
					</p>
					<p
						data-en="FireData is developed in Chihuahua, Mexico, by a multidisciplinary team for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026."
						data-es="FireData es desarrollado desde Chihuahua, Chihuahua, conformado por un equipo multidisciplinario para el NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026."
					>
						FireData is developed in Chihuahua, Mexico, by a multidisciplinary
						team for the NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026.
					</p>
				</div>
				<figure class="project-image">
					<img
						src="/images/sierra-chihuahua-map.png"
						alt="Map of Chihuahua showing the pilot monitoring area in the Sierra"
						data-en="Map of Chihuahua showing the pilot monitoring area in the Sierra"
						data-es="Mapa de Chihuahua con la zona piloto de monitoreo en la Sierra"
						loading="lazy"
					/>
					<figcaption
						data-en="Pilot area. Source: 2025 Intercensal Survey (EIC)"
						data-es="Ubicación del caso piloto. Fuente: Encuesta Intercensal (EIC) 2025"
					>
						Pilot area. Source: 2025 Intercensal Survey (EIC)
					</figcaption>
				</figure>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2 data-en="The team" data-es="El equipo">The team</h2>

			<article>
				<h3
					data-en="Data science and FIRMS"
					data-es="Ciencia de Datos y FIRMS"
				>
